00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:29.690
Well, it goes all over my
face otherwise, doesn't it, B?

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:33.350
Well, B, as you can see,

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:36.270
I've been having to make several
videos without you in them.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:37.420
And I'm sick of it,

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.580
to be honest, I've got no one
to talk to in these things.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:43.093
Aw, well, I'm sick of not being in them.

00:00:43.093 --> 00:00:45.650
I've just got no one to talk to, period.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:47.490
For those who don't know, Dan and I

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:50.167
for eight of the ten years
we've been doing this channel,

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:52.800
we've lived about 5,000 miles apart,

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:53.890
two different continents.

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:58.619
And currently due to
planetary pandemic situations,

00:00:58.619 --> 00:01:00.890
we can't travel to each other.

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:02.020
Technically I can go to England

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:05.270
but I have a real hard
time getting back here,

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:07.450
and then we don't have cameras in England

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.190
and you can only come
here if you're a diplomat,

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:11.023
right?

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:15.101
I think it's if you're
a diplomat, the queen

00:01:15.101 --> 00:01:16.130
or you're like American
or something like that.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:17.453
So I've had an idea,

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:21.840
we can't make videos during the pandemic

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.870
but there's nothing stopping us

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:26.293
from making a video before the pandemic.

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:32.290
I mean, I can think of a
couple of problems with that

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:34.440
Right? Go ahead.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:38.420
Firstly, that would require time travel.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:39.970
Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:42.650
So that would be the main problem.

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:44.330
You're 100 percent right.

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:46.670
I was thinking if any
YouTuber had a time machine

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.300
it would probably be Colin Furze,

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.890
and we've never made a
video with him before.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:51.470
He's always doing mad stuff.

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:54.510
So I think we'll get,
if we get hold of Colin

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:58.268
and then we'll just plan a
time when we were both free.

00:01:58.268 --> 00:01:59.130
Yeah.

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:01.270
It's very rare that we were both together

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:02.620
but not filming Slow-mo Guys.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:04.483
So when would be a good time?

00:02:05.469 --> 00:02:07.060
I know you came back to England

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:10.129
for a bit because you were
like, just wanted a rest.

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:13.660
Yeah. There was a time
between Super Slow Show

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:14.530
and Planet Slow-mo

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.620
where I just had a
restful week in England.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:19.105
We didn't film anything,
but we were both together.

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.200
Yeah.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.890
Just having a laugh.

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:23.910
If Colin was free that week.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:24.743
Perfect.

00:02:24.743 --> 00:02:26.000
I think that might work.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.100
We could sort out a Phantom
rental, nearby place.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.330
Should I give him a,
should I give him a bell?

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.163
Yeah. Give him a call.

00:02:32.163 --> 00:02:33.080
Alright, hold on.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.150
Hey, all right Colin? How's it going?

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:39.350
Hey, you all right
Slow-Mos? What we up to?

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:41.460
Wondering what the chances are of you

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:42.960
having a time machine.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:44.920
What's the time machine sitch?

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.077
Yeah. What's the time machine sitch?

00:02:47.077 --> 00:02:48.590
I've kind of got a time machine.

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:52.980
I've kind of got, I've got
well, maybe 50, 50% of it.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:54.410
50% better than nowt,

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:55.243
to be honest.

00:02:55.243 --> 00:02:57.240
Well, yeah. I mean
that's at least 50% more

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.020
of a time machine we've got.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:00.090
Full blown Delorean.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:01.890
Yeah, that's pretty sweet.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:04.502
Colin. We were wondering
about a cheeky collab.

00:03:04.502 --> 00:03:06.922
Are you free, or should I say

00:03:06.922 --> 00:03:11.922
were you free in November of 2017

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.110
November, 2017.

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:14.943
Let me think.

00:03:14.943 --> 00:03:16.019
All right.

00:03:16.019 --> 00:03:16.852
There will be a gap,

00:03:16.852 --> 00:03:19.020
when I was building the TIE
fighter up at Tom's farm.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:21.357
You come and see me then
and I think that would work.

00:03:21.357 --> 00:03:24.424
Brilliant, Colin, pick
us up when you're ready.

00:03:24.424 --> 00:03:26.117
Stick the kettle on, yeah?

00:03:26.117 --> 00:03:26.950
Excellent. Right?

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:29.570
I'll get it sorted and I'll
presume we had a lovely time,

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:31.675
well, I'll know in a minute, won't I?

00:03:31.675 --> 00:03:33.994
Yeah, yeah, I look forward to it, wait...

00:03:33.994 --> 00:03:35.470
Looked forward to it? No.

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:36.303
I don't know

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:40.420
Yeah, can't wait, couldn't wait.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.083
I couldn't have waited. What?

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:47.090
Hello. I'm Gav.
I'm Dan.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.120
We're the Slow-mo Guys

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:49.940
and today we're not in my back garden.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:52.140
In fact, you may realize
where we are already.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.350
We are in a prop shed though.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:54.183
That's true.

00:03:54.183 --> 00:03:55.016
Quite different from ours.

00:03:55.016 --> 00:03:55.859
Ours has, you know

00:03:55.859 --> 00:03:57.740
bits of string, balloons,
condoms, maybe a spade.

00:03:57.740 --> 00:04:00.290
This one's got Wolverine
claws, magnet boots

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:03.130
real mantles like lathes
and all sorts of cool stuff.

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:05.239
It also contains Colin Furze.

00:04:05.239 --> 00:04:07.666
Yes, me. How's it going?

00:04:07.666 --> 00:04:09.492
Thanks for having us Colin.

00:04:09.492 --> 00:04:11.360
It's a very famous room and I'm,

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:13.370
I'm delighted to be stood in it.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:14.740
So what we're going to
film today, in slow-mo?

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:17.183
Well. I've got one of these.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.600
Just casually lying around.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:21.020
The pulse jet engine.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:22.660
Now these things are super cool.

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:23.960
They make, like, loads of noise.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:25.150
They go red hot.

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:26.460
They spit fire out.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:27.293
They're awesome.

00:04:27.293 --> 00:04:28.920
But everyone always asks
me how do they work?

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.180
What's going on inside?

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:31.500
So I thought, well, you know,

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.240
you two could come in really handy here

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.110
It seems like we should
point one of these at it.

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:37.320
Phantom Flex 4K right through the window.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:38.153
Yep.

00:04:38.153 --> 00:04:39.060
You get a thousand frames a second easy.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:39.893
Sounds good.

00:04:39.893 --> 00:04:42.223
Are we doing it here in the shed?

00:04:42.223 --> 00:04:43.780
No, we are not doing it in here.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:47.030
Okay, good, good

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:48.050
Onward!

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.930
I'm bringing my cuppa.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:50.763
Jealous.

00:04:52.062 --> 00:04:52.895
Now we're in the field.

00:04:52.895 --> 00:04:55.250
Right? Look at this dry stone wall here.

00:04:55.250 --> 00:05:00.250
Lovely little view, ah,
the pulse jet engine.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:01.163
Here we are.

00:05:01.163 --> 00:05:02.940
Here we are then, pulse jet,

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:05.460
Slow-mo Guys got the
high speed camera set up

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:06.660
they don't know what's
going to happen yet,

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.160
he's just going to push the trigger when

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:10.137
he thinks he should do,
right, let's get it started.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:31.775
I felt like my heart,

00:05:31.775 --> 00:05:33.540
I bet if I was wearing a heart monitor

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:34.610
that would register.

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:37.390
I would say the term for it is it thrums.

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:38.223
Thrums!

00:05:38.223 --> 00:05:40.119
Yeah. I think that's the right word.

00:05:40.119 --> 00:05:42.617
It is kind of like the Eye of Mordor.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.314
Yeah, the Eye of Sauron

00:05:45.314 --> 00:05:46.344
Not sure I wanna look down there now.

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:51.550
For those of you who don't know

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.410
what the pulse jet actually is,

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:55.020
if you haven't seen Colin's videos

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:57.300
what it's doing is creating explosions

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:59.140
in this chamber and it sends a wave

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:01.072
of pressure out the long
and short ends of the tube.

00:06:01.072 --> 00:06:02.190
That's the jet part.

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:03.387
As the wave expands

00:06:03.387 --> 00:06:05.890
it leaves a near vacuum
behind in the chamber.

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:07.880
So fresh air and oxygen rush

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.046
in the short end and hot
gases are sucked back

00:06:10.046 --> 00:06:11.600
from the long end

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.209
which ignites a new burst of fuel.

00:06:13.209 --> 00:06:16.390
And the whole cycle repeats
itself, many times a second

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:18.220
which is why it's very
useful to be filming this

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:19.103
with the Phantom.

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:22.970
Shall we then now we've got that,

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:25.360
Should we try and rev it a bit harder?

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:26.560
Well, I'll rev it up a little bit.

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:28.780
Push the red button and
then switch it off, yeah?

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.680
Colin is now operating the Phantom

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:33.750
so we're not even needed, honestly.

00:06:44.208 --> 00:06:46.020
Fire always looks kind of CG to me

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:47.070
when it's this slow

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:48.653
this is 3000 frames a second.

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:51.840
It looks like it's just
going in one direction.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:53.330
But if I speed it up slightly

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:56.923
